  "abstract": "We prove sharp two-sided estimates for the finite-frame Schur correction associated with the first m pole-killing odd theta derivatives in a weighted realization of Weil's quadratic form. For each fixed m, its norm has order beta times log(1/beta) to the power 4m+5/2 as beta tends to zero, with explicit positive constants and a full small-parameter regime. The proof combines separate half-line charge cancellation, a square-root range construction, integrated full theta-tail control and matching odd box tests. We also prove a pointwise upper bound for low-energy gamma spectral mass and an exact change of metric after equality-space elimination. Prime powers and polar terms remain in the signed Weil reduction. No uniform growing-frame estimate, complementary-form positivity or solution of the Riemann Hypothesis is asserted.",
  "keywords": [
    "Riemann xi function",
    "theta kernel",
    "Weil quadratic form",
    "Schur complement",
    "weighted gamma operator",
    "resolvent estimates",
    "spectral measure"
  ],
